# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Git attributes — merge drivers for machine-generated files
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# blocked_ips.add / blocked_ips.submit are append-only, one-IP-per-line
# blocklists regenerated independently by the agent-nginx-threat-pipeline
# cron on MULTIPLE hosts. Without a merge driver, every pull/rebase where
# two hosts appended IPs conflicts (the classic blocked_ips.add conflict).
#
# `merge=union` is a built-in git driver: when both sides modify the file,
# the result is the concatenation of both versions — no conflict markers,
# no IPs lost. Duplicate lines are harmless (nginx deny dedupes implicitly
# and fix-blocked-ips.py tolerates them). The pipeline's own
# `git pull --rebase` retry now succeeds instead of aborting.
#
# Applied 2026-08-02 (Joseph) to eliminate blocked_ips.add pull conflicts.
ops/install/deploy/nginx/blocked_ips.add merge=union
ops/install/deploy/nginx/blocked_ips.submit merge=union
